{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted a command injection attack by appending a semicolon and the 'cat /etc/shadow' command to the 'host' parameter in a CGI script request. This technique attempts to execute arbitrary operating system commands on the target server. The HTTP 500 status code indicates that the server encountered an internal error while processing the request, potentially due to the malformed input or a crashed application process.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Execution",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Refactor the application code to avoid using shell-based execution functions (like system, exec, or popen) when handling user-supplied parameters.",
    "Implement strict input validation and allowlisting for the 'host' parameter, ensuring only valid IP addresses or domain names are accepted.",
    "Apply the principle of least privilege by running the web server and CGI scripts with restricted user permissions to prevent unauthorized access to sensitive system files like /etc/shadow."
  ]
}
